(c4) ()1. Ne[Be not very angry, O Lord, and remember no longer our iniquity:](f) i(g)ra(h)scá(hg)ris(h) Dó(ixhi)mi(h)ne,(h.) (,) 
ne(h) ul(h)tra(h) me(h)mí(h)ne(h)ris(h) i(g)ni(ixi)qui(h)tá(hg)tis:[/](f.) (:) 
ec[The city of Thy sanctuary is become a desert,](h)ce(ixi) cí(j)vi(j)tas(j) Sánc(j)ti(j_') fác(j)ta(j) est(j) de(j)sér(j)ta:(j.) (,) 
Sí[Sion is made a desert,](j)on(j) de(j)sér(jk)ta(j) fác(ixji)ta(h) est:[/](h.) (;) 
Je[Jerusalem is desolate,](f)rú(gh)sa(h)lem(h.) de(ixgi)so(h)lá(hg)ta(f) est:(f.) (:) 
dó[the house of Thy holiness,](h)mus(h) sanc(h)ti(h)fi(h)ca(h)ti(h)ó(h)nis(h) tú(h)ae(h_') 
et(h) gló[and of our glory,](h)ri(g)ae(j) tú(ixji)ae,(h.) (;) 
u[where our fathers praised Thee.](f)bi(gh) lau(h)da(h)vé(ixhi)runt(h) te(h.) pát(gf)res(e) nós(fe)tri.[/](d.) (::)
